    ○ today's reports  0.0KB  (no reports yet)
    ○ pinned reports   0.0KB  (none pinned)
    ○ history          0.0KB  (off · run $history)","hookSpecificOutput":{"hookEventName":"SessionStart","additionalContext":"<!-- agent static context · harness: codex · hooks and MCP server run from: <ROOT> · a write refused outside the home and its listed roots is policy, not a prompt: the operator lists the directory in .claude/settings.local.json permissions.additionalDirectories and runs $upgrade · delivered by the plugin's SessionStart hook because this host has no @-import -->

<!-- agentlayer glossary for codex: the skills are written in Claude Code's terms; read each one as follows -->
- \`\${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}\` → in one of agentlayer's skills (its \`<path>\` runs through \`agentlayer/<version>/skills/\`), \`<ROOT>\`, the checkout this session's hooks and MCP server run from, since that \`<path>\` is Codex's cached copy and can be an older version; in another plugin's skill, two folders above its SKILL.md
- \`\${CLAUDE_SKILL_DIR}\` → in one of agentlayer's skills, \`<ROOT>/skills/<skill>\` with the skill's name for \`<skill>\`; in another plugin's skill, the folder holding its SKILL.md
- \`mcp__plugin_agentlayer_agent__<tool>\` → \`mcp__agentlayer__<tool>\`, the same tool on this host's agentlayer MCP server
- \`AskUserQuestion\` → in Plan mode, \`request_user_input\`, which returns the answer as its result, so carry on; otherwise, and for a multi-select question, ask in chat (the question, then numbered options with the recommended one first), then end your turn and wait for the answer. Not \`request_user_input_async\`: Codex dismisses its card when your turn's final message renders
- \`Agent, a subagent\` → this host's subagent tool if it offers one (\`spawn_agent\`); otherwise do each part yourself, one after another, to the same output contract
- \`/agentlayer:<name> or Skill(agentlayer:<name>)\` → \`$<name>\`, the same skill run the way this host runs one
- \`WebSearch\` → this host's web search, or the agent's \`web_search\` tool
- \`WebFetch\` → this host's page fetch, or \`curl\`

